---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Design Journey — Learning Fashion Design from the Ground Up" description="Documenting Nancy Wambui's progression from understanding clothing to learning fashion design, pattern drafting, garment construction, and sewing-machine prototyping.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">DESIGN JOURNEY</p>
        <h1>From Understanding Clothing to Learning How to Create It</h1>
        <p>
          SmartLukuFitness began with practical styling and personal presentation. The natural next step is going deeper — learning fashion design, garment construction, pattern drafting, and machine sewing from the ground up, and documenting every lesson along the way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <p class="eyebrow">Transparent Learning Journal</p>
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0.3rem;">An Honest Development Story</h2>
        <p>
          This is a public learning notebook, not a commercial fashion house or brand launch. There are no products for sale, no pre-made collections, and no claims of established designer status. It is a real, step-by-step account of learning a craft through study, practice, mistakes, and iteration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The 4-phase framework</p>
        <h2>How the Journey Unfolds</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="pillar-grid" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <article class="pillar-card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Phase 1</span>
          <h3>1. Learn</h3>
          <p>Studying fashion theory, garment history, silhouette balance, fabric characteristics, seam structures, and pattern drafting fundamentals for men's and women's wear.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar-card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Phase 2</span>
          <h3>2. Experiment</h3>
          <p>Building mood boards, fashion sketching, exploring color stories, testing fabric drape, and turning visual inspiration into original garment concepts.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar-card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Phase 3</span>
          <h3>3. Make</h3>
          <p>Hands-on sewing machine practice, straight-line stitching exercises, seam finishing, pattern cutting, basic samples, and prototyping initial garments.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar-card" style="grid-column: span 1;">
          <span class="card-kicker">Phase 4</span>
          <h3>4. Develop</h3>
          <p>Refining construction techniques, analyzing sample mistakes, adjusting fit, and slowly turning successful prototypes into original clothing pieces over time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="padding: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; background: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Sewing Machine &amp; Workshop Timeline</h3>
        <p>
          Hands-on machine practice and physical sample creation will begin as workshop equipment is set up around early December. In the meantime, focus remains on fashion theory, pattern drafting concepts, fabric research, and visual sketching.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p>
        <h2>Journal Topics &amp; Future Notes</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Fabric Knowledge &amp; Behaviour</h3>
          <p>Notes on natural vs. synthetic fabrics, weave structures, stretch behavior, and selecting the right material for structured office wear.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Pattern Drafting Essentials</h3>
          <p>Understanding bodices, shirt blocks, trouser drafts, seam allowances, and how 2D flat patterns become 3D garments.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Machine Stitching &amp; Techniques</h3>
          <p>Documenting tension adjustments, straight seams, curved stitching, seam finishes, hem construction, and early machine practice.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Construction Lessons &amp; Failures</h3>
          <p>Honest breakdowns of misaligned seams, puckered fabrics, fit issues, and what each mistake teaches about proper construction.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/style/`} class="btn btn-secondary">← Explore Style Guides</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
